# THE VISUAL VOCABULARY
#
# SHOWS: all seven types, all eight shapes, and advisory typing.
#
# Every type has a colour, an icon, a default shape, and named slots. Notice
# that `character -> location` connects but draws DASHED and counts as a
# mismatch in the status bar. It is allowed. In a narrative graph the wrong
# edge is often the interesting one.
#
# Try the palette dropdown. Try overriding a shape in the inspector.

palette contrast

node act1     "Act One"           type:scene
node cellar   "The Cellar"        type:location
node borlu    "Borlu"             type:character
node poem     "Ascent of Prometheus" type:lore
     frag:"a subtraction that was never anywhere"
node pen      "The Red Pen"       type:object
node nightmare "The Same Corridor" type:dream
     frag:"the doors were not where you left them"
node todo     "check the ledger dates" type:note

# shape overrides — same type, different shape
node fork     "A Decision"        type:scene shape:diamond
node coin     "A Token"           type:scene shape:circle
node banner   "A Proclamation"    type:scene shape:slab

# sensible connections
act1   -> cellar    : go down
cellar -> act1      : back up the stairs
pen    -> act1      : carry it with you
poem   -> act1      : informs
borlu  -> act1      : appears in
act1   -> nightmare : sleep
nightmare -> act1   : wake

# structure demo
act1 -> fork   : reach the choice
fork -> coin   : take the token
fork -> banner : read the notice
coin   -> act1 : back
banner -> act1 : back

# DELIBERATELY WRONG — character into location. dashed, counted, permitted.
# this is the ONLY mismatch in the file. everything else fits.
borlu -> cellar : follow him down

# an object feeding a scene, which the type system likes
pen -> nightmare : it turns up in the dream

todo -> act1 : (a note, never rendered)
